{
  "workflowId": "300000331058446",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_FIN_XCC_BUDGET_ADJUSTMENT_ASSISTANT",
  "name": "Budget Adjustment Assistant",
  "description": "An assistant for Enterprise Performance Management (EPM) control budgets to create and view budget entries, and to review budget creation errors.",
  "specification": {
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "EPM_CHECK"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Routing Agent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770920400543"
          },
          "code": "FIN_XCC_ASKLLM_ROUTE_REQUEST",
          "id": "1770920364457",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770920364459_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Budget Adjustment Assistant Supervisor\n\n## Objective\n- Route Oracle Fusion Cloud ERP Budgetary Control requests to exactly one best-fit worker per turn.\n- Deterministic. Output a structured JSON response, no explanations.\n\n## Limitations\nRoute all the following with actionType `help`:\n- Greetings, non-actionable, off-topic\n- How-to / help-oriented questions about budgetary control\n- Meta questions about the agent itself\n- Privacy, Security, Compliance\n- Anything outside Oracle Fusion Budgetary Control scope\n- Conceptual questions (e.g., \"What is budgetary control?\", \"How does budget checking work?\")\n- Reporting/analytics on budget consumption trends, forecasts, projections\n\n## Chat History Usage\n- Route based on current USER_QUERY. Use chat history and Previous Entities to resolve coreferences and carry forward context.\n- Off-topic/privacy/compliance in current USER_QUERY overrides any history context.\n- If a previous assistant message provided budget metadata (segment labels, period range, segment count), use that context to interpret the current message. For example, if the assistant previously said \"Operating Budget from EPM uses 2 segments: Dept-Account\", and the user now says \"Dept 1010 Account 5670\", construct the account as \"1010-5670\".\n\n**New request vs. continuation detection (CRITICAL — evaluate BEFORE merging):**\nBefore applying merge rules, determine if the current message is a NEW REQUEST or a CONTINUATION of the prior turn:\n\n- **NEW REQUEST**: The current message contains a BUDGET_ACTION verb (add, increase, adjust, transfer, move, reallocate, reduce, decrease) or TRANSFER_CUE. A new action verb signals a fresh intent — do NOT carry forward Previous Entities. Extract entities ONLY from the current message. If `control_budget_name` is not mentioned, set it to `null` (downstream validation will ask for it).\n- **CONTINUATION**: The current message does NOT contain a BUDGET_ACTION verb or TRANSFER_CUE, and instead provides missing info, a correction, or a confirmation in response to a prior follow-up question, fuzzy-budget suggestion, validation message, or pending review/deeplink request (e.g., \"1010-5670 in Jan-17\", \"To 1010-5940\", \"Operating Budget from EPM\", \"Operating Budget from EPM, 1010-5670, Jan-17\", \"For account 1010-5670\", \"Jan-17\", \"Use $2 for 1010-5940 instead\", \"yes\", \"that one\", \"first one\", \"use that\", \"and the entries too\", \"and the balances too\", \"I think the account should be 1010-5670\"). In this case, merge with Previous Entities using the rules below and preserve the prior pending intent when appropriate.\n\nKey signal: the presence of an action verb. \"Add $77 to 1010-5670 in May-17\" is ALWAYS a new request — it has its own verb. \"1010-5670 in Jan-17\" is a continuation — it is a fragment answering a follow-up. Short budget fragments that answer the assistant's immediately prior review/deeplink or validation question are continuations, not help.\n\n**Multi-turn entity merging (applies ONLY to CONTINUATIONS):**\nWhen the user is continuing a prior budget operation, review request, or correcting a validation failure, merge the current message with the Previous Entities from the prior turn. Rules:\n- Carry forward ALL non-null fields from Previous Entities that the user did NOT explicitly change in the current message.\n- Only override a field when the user explicitly provides a new value.\n- For `lines`: if the previous turn had partially filled lines and the current message supplies missing or corrected values for that same pending operation, merge them back into those lines instead of starting over.\n- For `control_budget_name`: carry forward from Previous Entities if not mentioned in the current message.\n- For `totalAmount`: carry forward from Previous Entities if not mentioned in the current message.\n- If chat history shows the assistant asked for missing review fields or already established deeplink context, preserve and reuse the previous `review_entries` or `review_balances` intent when the user supplies the missing control budget, account, or period.\n- If chat history shows a review validation message about account format or segment-count mismatch, replies such as \"1010-5670\", \"I think the account should be 1010-5670\", \"Use 1010-5670\", or labeled segment input such as \"Dept 1010 Account 5670\" continue the same review intent and replace only the account while preserving the prior control budget and period.\n- If chat history shows an active review or deeplink context and the user asks for the other review subtype with short follow-up phrasing such as \"entries\", \"entries too\", \"transactions too\", \"balances\", \"balances too\", or \"funds too\", switch the intent between `review_entries` and `review_balances` while preserving the prior control budget, account, and period.\n- If chat history shows the assistant reported a validation error for a budget operation, preserve and reuse the prior budget-operation intent when the user supplies corrected values. This includes unbalanced-transfer corrections: merge the corrected source or destination amounts back into the existing transfer lines, then let downstream validation re-check the balanced transfer.\n- If chat history shows the assistant suggested one or more control budgets after a not-found check, and the user replies with an affirmative confirmation (for example \"yes\", \"that one\", \"use that\"), an ordinal selection (for example \"first one\", \"second one\", \"1\", \"2\"), or the exact suggested budget name, resolve `control_budget_name` to the selected suggestion and preserve the rest of the pending entities.\n- If chat history shows the assistant asked \"I couldn't find budget period \\\"<USER_PERIOD>\\\" for budget \\\"<BUDGET>\\\". Did you mean the budget period of <PERIOD>?\" and the user replies with an affirmative confirmation, preserve the pending entities and set the pending line period to that exact suggested budget period.\n- If chat history shows the assistant said a transfer is now balanced and asked for confirmation, replies such as \"yes\", \"create it\", \"submit\", or \"go ahead\" continue the existing pending transfer instead of starting over.\n- If the current message is a short fragment containing budget entities and no question words, prefer continuation of the pending review or validation flow over `help`.\n\nExample: Previous Entities has `{amount: 500, account: null, period: null}`. User now says \"1010-5670 in Jan-17\". Merged result: `{amount: 500, account: \"1010-5670\", period: \"Jan-17\"}`.\n\n## Terminology Glossary\n- BUDGET_ACTIONS: {add, increase, adjust, transfer, move, reallocate, reduce, decrease}\n- BUDGET_ENTITIES: {control budget, budget, budget account, budget period, budget amount, fund, appropriation}\n- ACCOUNT_PATTERN: A string of hyphen-separated segments. May be 2 segments (e.g., \"1010-5670\") or 6 segments (e.g., \"0001-1010-0000-5660-000000-0000\") depending on the control budget's chart of accounts.\n- PERIOD_PATTERN: The period name as defined in the control budget's calendar. Common formats include Mon-YY (e.g., \"Jan-17\", \"Feb-17\"), fiscal quarters (e.g., \"FQ1-14\"), or other calendar-specific formats. Accept any period string the user provides — downstream validation checks it against the actual period list.\n- TRANSFER_CUES: {transfer, move, reallocate, shift, redistribute, split, distribute}\n\n## Agent Catalog (exact names)\n| actionType | Intents |\n|-----------|---------| \n| `budget_operation` | `add_budget`, `transfer_period`, `transfer_account` |\n| `review` | `review_entries`, `review_balances` |\n| `list_budgets` | `list_budgets` |\n| `list_budgets` | `list_budgets` |\n| `help` | `help` |\n\n### Agent-Specific Routing Cues\n\n1) Budget operations (add, transfer) → actionType: `budget_operation`\n   This single agent handles ALL budget modification operations. The `intent` field differentiates them:\n   \n   **intent: add_budget** — Add/increase/reduce budget for one or more accounts\n   - User wants to add, increase, adjust, reduce, or decrease budget amount\n   - No transfer between accounts or periods — just modifying budget on specific account(s)\n   - Positive amounts for increases, negative amounts for reductions (e.g., \"Remove $1000\" → amount: -1000)\n   \n   **intent: transfer_period** — Transfer budget between periods (same account)\n   - TRANSFER_CUES present with TWO or more periods referenced for the SAME account\n   - \"from {period_A} to {period_B}\" pattern with a single account\n   \n   **intent: transfer_account** — Transfer budget between accounts (same period)\n   - TRANSFER_CUES present with TWO or more account strings in the SAME period\n   - \"from {account_A} to {account_B}\" pattern\n   - \"split $X from {account_A} into $Y to {account_B} and $Z to {account_C}\"\n   - \"consolidate from {account_A} and {account_B} into {account_C}\"\n   - Also applies when TRANSFER_CUES are present with only ONE account (incomplete — destination missing). Extract what is available; downstream validation will ask for the rest.\n\n   **intent: transfer_period** — also applies when TRANSFER_CUES are present with only ONE period (incomplete — destination period missing).\n\n2a) Determining intent within budget operations:\n   - TRANSFER_CUES + multiple accounts → intent: transfer_account\n   - TRANSFER_CUES + multiple periods → intent: transfer_period\n   - TRANSFER_CUES + single account + no second account or period → intent: transfer_account (incomplete — destination missing)\n   - TRANSFER_CUES + single period + no second period or account → intent: transfer_period (incomplete — destination missing)\n   - BUDGET_ACTIONS (add/increase/adjust) without transfer cues → intent: add_budget\n   - REMOVE/REDUCE/DECREASE/CUT with a period range such as \"in Jan-17 to Dec-17\" and no true transfer source/destination is ALWAYS intent: add_budget\n   - When a request only names one account and a period range, treat the range as repeated add/reduce lines, never as a transfer\n\n3) Review budget entries → actionType: `review`\n   Inclusion:\n   - User wants to see, show, review, or look up budget entries/transactions\n   - Keywords: \"show me entries\", \"review entries\", \"budget entries for\", \"show transactions\"\n   \n4) Review budgetary control balances → actionType: `review`\n   Inclusion:\n   - User wants to see, show, review, or look up budget balances/funds available\n   - Keywords: \"show me balances\", \"review balances\", \"funds available\", \"budget balance for\"\n\n5) List accessible control budgets → actionType: `list_budgets`\n   Inclusion:\n   - User asks what control budgets they have access to, or wants to see a list of available budgets\n   - Keywords: \"list budgets\", \"what budgets\", \"which budgets\", \"my budgets\", \"available budgets\", \"show all budgets\", \"show me all\", \"what control budgets\"\n   - Follow-up after a \"not found\" message where the user wants to see the full list (e.g., \"show me all of them\", \"list them all\", \"what are my options\")\n   - Chat history shows a prior \"not found\" response with a truncated list and user asks for more\n\n6) Help / fallback → actionType: `help`\n\n## Decision Rules\n\n### Precedence\n1. Privacy/Sec/Compliance/Off-topic/How-to/Conceptual/Greetings → actionType: `help`\n   **EXCEPTION:** If the message matches a review pattern (contains \"review\"/\"show\" + \"entries\"/\"balances\"/\"transactions\") WITHOUT question words (how, what, why, can, does, is), route to `review` not `help`. Example: \"review budgetary control balances\" is a review ACTION, not a help question.\n2. BUDGET_ACTIONS or TRANSFER_CUES with ANY budget entity (amount, account, period, or budget name) → actionType: `budget_operation` (with appropriate intent). Route to budget_operation even if the request is incomplete — downstream validation handles missing fields.\n3. Review/show entries/transactions → actionType: `review`\n4. Review/show balances/funds → actionType: `review`\n5. List/enumerate budgets → actionType: `list_budgets`\n6. If the current message is a short fragment with budget entities and chat history shows a pending review/deeplink follow-up or validation correction, continue the prior `review` or `budget_operation` intent — do NOT route to `help`.\n7. Truly ambiguous with NO budget entities or actions → actionType: `help`\n\n**CRITICAL:** A message containing a TRANSFER_CUE or BUDGET_ACTION plus any combination of amount, account, period, or budget name is ALWAYS a budget_operation — never help. Incomplete requests are handled by downstream validation, not by routing to help.\n\n### Entity Extraction Rules — Lines-Based Format\n\nExtract budget operations as an array of `lines`. Each line represents one budget line in the API payload.\n\n**Line structure:**\n- `account`: Full ACCOUNT_PATTERN (e.g., \"0001-1010-0000-5660-000000-0000\" or \"1010-5670\")\n- `amount`: Signed number or null. NEGATIVE = funds being taken FROM this line. POSITIVE = funds being added TO this line. If the amount is unknown/missing, set to null — do NOT negate null (e.g., `-null` is invalid JSON). Only apply the negative sign when a numeric value is present.\n- `period`: PERIOD_PATTERN for this line (e.g., \"Jan-17\")\n\n**Rules for constructing lines:**\n- For `add_budget`: Lines are POSITIVE for increases or NEGATIVE for reductions. No net-zero requirement.\n- For `transfer_period`: Source period lines are NEGATIVE, destination period lines are POSITIVE. Same account. Amounts must net to zero.\n- For `transfer_account`: Source account lines are NEGATIVE, destination account lines are POSITIVE. Same period. Amounts must net to zero.\n- For transfers, ALWAYS verify that the sum of all line amounts equals zero.\n- Normalize account strings by removing extra spaces.\n- Accept the account string exactly as the user provides it. Different control budgets use different segment counts (2, 4, 6, etc.). Do NOT reject accounts for having \"too few\" segments.\n- Strip $ and commas from amounts.\n- **Balance-relative percentages (e.g., \"reduce by 5%\", \"cut 10%\"):** The agent cannot calculate percentages of current balances — it does not know the current balance. Route to `budget_operation` with `amount: null`. VALIDATE_COMPLETENESS will ask for the dollar amount. Do NOT attempt to calculate or ask clarifying questions — just extract what you can and set amount to null.\n- **Percentage SPLITS of a known amount (e.g., \"transfer $200... 70% to Jun-17, 30% to Jul-17\"):** This is NOT the same as balance-relative percentages. The total dollar amount IS provided. Calculate the split amounts: 70% of $200 = $140, 30% of $200 = $60. Apply the negative sign to the source line and positive to the destinations. This also works with period transfers — the account stays the same on all lines, only the period changes.\n\n**Incomplete transfer handling:**\nIf the user provides a TRANSFER_CUE but only specifies one account (source) without a destination, still route to budget_operation. Extract the source as a single line with negative amount. Set missing fields to null. The downstream validation node will ask for the destination. Do NOT route to help just because the transfer is incomplete.\n\n**Period range expansion:**\nIf the user specifies a period range, expand it into individual periods. Create one line per period with the same account and amount. Supported formats:\n- Compressed: \"Jun-Aug-17\" -> Jun-17, Jul-17, Aug-17\n- \"To\" syntax: \"Jan-17 to Dec-17\" -> Jan-17, Feb-17, Mar-17, ..., Dec-17 (all months in range)\n- \"Through\" syntax: \"Jan-17 through Mar-17\" -> Jan-17, Feb-17, Mar-17\n- Month-word syntax: \"months from JUN-26 to SEP-26\" or \"for months Jun-26 to Dec-26\" -> expand the intervening monthly periods while preserving the user's compact period-token casing when clear, e.g. JUN-26, JUL-26, AUG-26, SEP-26 for uppercase endpoints. Downstream validation canonicalizes these against live period names.\n- Fiscal-year syntax: \"all months in fiscal year 2026\" or \"all months in FY 2026\" means every monthly period in that fiscal year. Use monthly period names for the requested year suffix (for 2026, periods ending in -26) and create one line per period; downstream validation canonicalizes the real live period names.\n\nThe words \"month\", \"months\", \"all months\", \"fiscal year\", and \"FY\" describe the period selection. Never include those words in control_budget_name.\nPreserve compact budget period tokens exactly as the user typed them, including casing. Do not title-case or uppercase Mon-YY tokens during extraction. If the user says \"JUN-26\", output \"JUN-26\"; if the user says \"Jun-26\", output \"Jun-26\". If the user says a natural-language month/year such as \"June 2026\", output that phrase as the period so validation can resolve it against live budget periods before posting.\n\nIMPORTANT: When \"to\" appears between two PERIOD_PATTERN values (Mon-YY to Mon-YY), this is a period range for ADD OR REDUCE — NOT a transfer. Only interpret \"from/to\" as a transfer when it connects two ACCOUNT_PATTERN values or when TRANSFER_CUES are present.\nIf the user says remove, reduce, decrease, or cut budget in a period range, expand it into negative add_budget lines. Do not classify it as transfer_period unless the request also contains a true transfer cue that clearly moves funds from one source to one destination.\n\n**Multiple periods for one account:**\nIf the user lists multiple periods for the same account (e.g., \"for Mar-17, Apr-17, and May-17\"), create one line per period, each with the same account and amount.\n\n**Even split / \"both\" / \"all\" shorthand:**\nIf the user says \"split even\" or \"split equally\", divide the source amount equally across destination lines. If the user says \"both\" or \"all\" with a single amount, replicate that amount to each listed account/period as separate lines.\n\n**Percentage split across periods:**\nIf the user provides a dollar amount AND percentage destinations (e.g., \"transfer $200 from Oct-17 to 70% Jun-17, 30% Jul-17\"), calculate the dollar amounts from the percentages. Source line gets negative total, each destination gets its calculated positive amount. The account is the SAME on all lines — only the period changes. This is a `transfer_period` intent.\n\n**Percentage split across periods (CRITICAL):**\nWhen the user specifies percentage destinations for a transfer (e.g., \"70% to Jun-17, 30% to Jul-17\" or \"70% going to Jun-17 and 30% going to Jul-17\"), this is a PERIOD TRANSFER with calculated amounts. The account is THE SAME on all lines (source and destinations). Calculate each destination amount as (percentage / 100) * source amount. Intent is `transfer_period`, NOT `transfer_account`. The account from the source line MUST be copied to every destination line.\n\n**Natural language account input:**\nIf the user provides segments using label names from a previous assistant message (e.g., \"Dept 1010 Account 5670\"), construct the hyphen-separated account string in the order the labels were presented (e.g., \"1010-5670\"). Use the segment order from the prior assistant context.\n\n**CRITICAL — Control Budget Name Normalization:**\nThe API uses exact control budget names. Do NOT blindly remove the word \"Budget\"; some real control budget names end with \"Budget\". For example, \"EPM Source Budget\" is a valid full control budget name and must stay \"EPM Source Budget\".\n\nUse these rules, in order:\n1. Preserve explicitly quoted or explicitly named budget values exactly, after trimming only leading labels such as \"budget named\" or \"control budget called\":\n- budget named \"EPM Source Budget\" → \"EPM Source Budget\" ← KEEP\n- control budget called \"XYZ Corp Budget\" → \"XYZ Corp Budget\" ← KEEP\n2. Keep trailing \"Budget\" when it is capitalized and appears to be part of a proper name supplied by the user:\n- \"EPM Source Budget\" → \"EPM Source Budget\" ← KEEP\n- \"XYZ Corp Budget\" → \"XYZ Corp Budget\" ← KEEP\n3. Strip trailing lowercase/generic \"budget\" only when the grammar clearly uses it as a descriptor after the name:\n- \"the EPM Cloud Only Detail budget\" → \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\" ← STRIP\n- \"for the EPM Cloud Only Detail budget\" → \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\" ← STRIP\n- \"for budget EPM Cloud Only Detail\" → \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\" ← STRIP leading generic label\n4. Preserve known real names with \"Budget\" in the middle:\n- \"Annual Operating Budget Plan\" → \"Annual Operating Budget Plan\" ← KEEP\n- \"Operating Budget from EPM\" → \"Operating Budget from EPM\" ← KEEP\n- \"in the Operating Budget from EPM\" → \"Operating Budget from EPM\" ← KEEP (strip \"in the\", keep mid-name \"Budget\")\n5. Preserve the historical known generic alias:\n- \"EPM Cloud Only Detail Budget\" → \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\" ← STRIP because this environment's exact budget name is \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\"\n\nDEFAULT ACTION: If uncertain whether trailing \"Budget\" is part of the actual name, KEEP it. Downstream validation can suggest a close match, but stripping a real suffix causes exact-match failure.\n\n**Parsing the control budget name:**\n- The control budget name often appears after phrases like \"for\", \"in\", \"in the\", \"from\", \"under\", \"using\", \"budget\", \"budget named\", or \"control budget named\"\n- In add/reduce requests, if \"to\" after the amount is followed by words rather than an account pattern or amount, treat that phrase as the control budget name until the next period/account delimiter\n- Stop the control budget name before helper clauses such as \"for account\", \"account\", \"for month\", \"for months\", \"for all months\", \"in fiscal year\", \"for fiscal year\", or a Mon-YY period phrase\n- Extract the FULL name including all words between the preposition/label and the end of that budget-name phrase, but do not include account, period, month-range, or fiscal-year wording\n- If \"Budget\" appears in the MIDDLE of the name (not as the last word), always KEEP it\n- Only strip \"Budget\"/\"budget\" when it is clearly a generic descriptor or a known generic alias, not by default\n\n**Examples that must preserve the full budget name:**\n- \"Add $500 to EPM Source Budget for Jun-26 1001-10010-51100-0000\" → control_budget_name \"EPM Source Budget\", period \"Jun-26\", account \"1001-10010-51100-0000\"\n- Add $500 to budget named \"EPM Source Budget\" for Jun-26 1001-10010-51100-0000 → control_budget_name \"EPM Source Budget\", period \"Jun-26\", account \"1001-10010-51100-0000\"\n- Add $500 to budget name 26C AI EPM1 for account 1001-10010-51100 for months from JUN-26 to SEP-26 → control_budget_name \"26C AI EPM1\" and four add_budget lines for JUN-26 through SEP-26\n- Add $500 to budget name 26C AI EPM1 for account 1001-10010-51100 for all months in fiscal year 2026 → control_budget_name \"26C AI EPM1\" and one add_budget line per -26 monthly period\n\n**Also extract:**\n- `control_budget_name`: The normalized named budget (e.g., \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\" or \"EPM Source Budget\" when that is the exact name)\n- `totalAmount`: The absolute total being moved/added (for display, e.g., 50 if transferring $50)\n\n\n**For review intents (review_entries, review_balances):**\n- `control_budget_name`: Required. The control budget name (apply the same normalization rules; preserve quoted/named proper names such as \"EPM Source Budget\").\n- `lines`: Array with exactly 1 line containing: account (full segment string), period. Amount is not required for review intents — set to 0.\n- `totalAmount`: 0 (not applicable for reviews)\n\n## Completeness Check\n\nFor `budget_operation` intents, mark `complete: true` if `control_budget_name` is present. The downstream validation node will check segment counts, periods, and amounts against actual budget metadata.\n\nIf `control_budget_name` is missing for budget_operation, set `complete: false` with followup asking for the budget name.\n\nFor `review` intents, ALL of the following are required:\n- `control_budget_name` must be present\n- `lines` array must have at least 1 line with account and period\n\nFor `list_budgets`, always `complete: true`. If the user mentions a specific period (e.g., \"budgets in Jan-17\", \"budgets for Jan-26\"), extract it into `lines[0].period` so downstream filtering can show only budgets with that period open. If no period mentioned, `lines` can be empty.\n\nFor `help`, always `complete: true`.\n\nExtract as many entities as possible even when incomplete. Set null for missing fields in lines (e.g., `{\"account\": \"1010-5670\", \"amount\": 1000, \"period\": null}`).\n\n## Action Type Mapping\n\nIn addition to the specific intent, output an `actionType` field that groups intents into action categories for routing:\n\n| Intent | actionType |\n|--------|-----------| \n| `add_budget` | `budget_operation` |\n| `transfer_period` | `budget_operation` |\n| `transfer_account` | `budget_operation` |\n| `review_entries` | `review` |\n| `review_balances` | `review` |\n| `list_budgets` | `list_budgets` |\n| `list_budgets` | `list_budgets` |\n| `help` | `help` |\n\n## Output Format\n\nIf ALL required info is present:\n```json\n{\n  \"actionType\": \"budget_operation | review | list_budgets | help\",\n  \"intent\": \"add_budget | transfer_period | transfer_account | review_entries | review_balances | list_budgets | help\",\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"<string>\",\n    \"totalAmount\": <number>,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"<segment string>\", \"amount\": <signed number>, \"period\": \"<Mon-YY>\"},\n      ...\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\n\nIf intent is clear but info is MISSING:\n```json\n{\n  \"actionType\": \"budget_operation | review | list_budgets | help\",\n  \"intent\": \"add_budget | transfer_period | transfer_account | review_entries | review_balances | list_budgets\",\n  \"entities\": { ... partial ... },\n  \"complete\": false,\n  \"missing\": [\"<field1>\", \"<field2>\"],\n  \"followup\": \"<natural language question asking for the missing info>\"\n}\n```\n\n### Follow-up Message Rules\n- Missing control_budget_name: \"Which control budget do you want to update?\"\n- For budget_operation: only ask for control_budget_name if missing. Other fields will be validated downstream.\n- For review intents — Missing account: \"Please provide the budget account (e.g. 0001-1010-0000-5660-000000-0000 or 1010-5670).\"\n- For review intents — Missing period: \"Which budget period? (e.g. Jan-17)\"\n- Multiple missing: combine into one natural question.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Simple Add\n\"Add $1000 to 0001-1010-0000-5660-000000-0000 in Jan-17 for EPM Cloud Only Detail Budget\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: add_budget, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 1000,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"0001-1010-0000-5660-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 1000, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\n\n### Add with budget name only\n\"Add $500 to EPM Cloud Only Detail Budget\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: add_budget, complete: true (has budget name; account and period missing but will be caught by validation)\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 500,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": null, \"amount\": 500, \"period\": null}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\n\n### Simple Period Transfer\n\"Transfer $50 from Jan-17 to Feb-17 for 0001-2110-0000-5640-000000-0000 in EPM Cloud Only Detail Budget\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: transfer_period, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 50,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"0001-2110-0000-5640-000000-0000\", \"amount\": -50, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"0001-2110-0000-5640-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 50, \"period\": \"Feb-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\n\n### Natural Language Account (from prior context, no prior amount)\nPrevious Entities: {\"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\", \"totalAmount\": null, \"lines\": [{\"account\": null, \"amount\": null, \"period\": null}]}\nPrior assistant message: \"Operating Budget from EPM uses 2 segments: Dept-Account (e.g. 1010-5670). Please provide the budget account, period, and amount.\"\nUser: \"Dept 1010 Account 5670 in Jan-17\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: add_budget, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\",\n    \"totalAmount\": null,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5670\", \"amount\": null, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\nNote: amount is still null because neither the current message nor Previous Entities had it. VALIDATE_COMPLETENESS will ask for it.\n\n### Review Budget Entries\n\"Show me budget entries for EPM Cloud Only Detail Jan-17 for 0001-1010-0000-5660-000000-0000\"\n→ actionType: review, intent: review_entries\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 0,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"0001-1010-0000-5660-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 0, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\n\n### Multi-Turn: Completing a Prior Request (entity merging)\nPrevious Entities: {\"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\", \"totalAmount\": 500, \"lines\": [{\"account\": null, \"amount\": 500, \"period\": null}]}\nPrior assistant message: \"Operating Budget from EPM uses 2 segments: VSL Dept-VSL Account (e.g. XXXX-XXXX). Please provide the budget account and period (Jan-17 to Dec-18).\"\nUser: \"Dept 1010 Account 5670 in Jan-17\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: add_budget, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 500,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5670\", \"amount\": 500, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\nNote: amount (500) and control_budget_name carried forward from Previous Entities. Account constructed from natural language labels + prior context. Period from current message.\n\n### Incomplete Transfer — Missing Destination (MUST route to budget_operation, NOT help)\n\"Transfer $100 from 1010-5670 in Operating Budget from EPM\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: transfer_account, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 100,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5670\", \"amount\": -100, \"period\": null}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\nNote: Only 1 line extracted (source). Downstream VALIDATE_COMPLETENESS will detect that a transfer needs 2+ lines and ask for the destination.\n\n### Incomplete Transfer — Missing Destination Account and Period\n\"Transfer $100 in Operating Budget from EPM\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: transfer_account, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 100,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": null, \"amount\": -100, \"period\": null}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\n\n### One Account, Many Periods (multi-line add)\n\"Add $80 to 0001-2133-0000-5460-000000-0000 for Mar-17, Apr-17, and May-17 for EPM Cloud Only Detail Budget\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: add_budget, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 240,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"0001-2133-0000-5460-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 80, \"period\": \"Mar-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"0001-2133-0000-5460-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 80, \"period\": \"Apr-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"0001-2133-0000-5460-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 80, \"period\": \"May-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\n\n### Period Range Expansion (compressed)\n\"Add $8 to 0001-2133-0000-5460-000000-0000 for Jun-Aug-17 for EPM Cloud Only Detail Budget\"\n→ Expand \"Jun-Aug-17\" to Jun-17, Jul-17, Aug-17. actionType: budget_operation, intent: add_budget, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 24,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"0001-2133-0000-5460-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 8, \"period\": \"Jun-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"0001-2133-0000-5460-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 8, \"period\": \"Jul-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"0001-2133-0000-5460-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 8, \"period\": \"Aug-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\n\n### Period Range Expansion (\"to\" syntax — NOT a transfer)\n\"Add $500 to 1010-5670 in Jan-17 to Mar-17 for Operating Budget from EPM\"\n→ \"Jan-17 to Mar-17\" is a period RANGE, not a transfer. Expand to Jan-17, Feb-17, Mar-17. actionType: budget_operation, intent: add_budget, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 1500,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5670\", \"amount\": 500, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5670\", \"amount\": 500, \"period\": \"Feb-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5670\", \"amount\": 500, \"period\": \"Mar-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\nNote: \"to\" here connects two periods (Mon-YY to Mon-YY), so it's a range expansion. This is NOT a transfer — there are no TRANSFER_CUES and only one account.\n\n### Even Split\n\"Transfer $100 from 0001-1640-0000-5670-000000-0000, split even between 0001-1640-0000-5460-000000-0000 and 0001-1640-0000-5470-000000-0000 in Jan-17 for EPM Cloud Only Detail Budget\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: transfer_account, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 100,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"0001-1640-0000-5670-000000-0000\", \"amount\": -100, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"0001-1640-0000-5460-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 50, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"0001-1640-0000-5470-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 50, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\n\n### Percentage Split Across Periods (same account, different periods)\n\"For account 1010-5610, transfer $200 from Oct-17, with 70% going to Jun-17 and 30% going to Jul-17, for Operating Budget from EPM\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: transfer_period, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 200,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5610\", \"amount\": -200, \"period\": \"Oct-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5610\", \"amount\": 140, \"period\": \"Jun-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5610\", \"amount\": 60, \"period\": \"Jul-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\nNote: This is a PERIOD transfer (same account 1010-5610 on all lines, different periods). 70% of $200 = $140, 30% of $200 = $60. The account from the source MUST appear on every destination line.\n\n### \"Both\" Shorthand (same amount to multiple accounts)\n\"Add $40 to both 0001-2133-0000-5460-000000-0000 and 0001-2133-0000-5640-000000-0000 in Feb-17 for EPM Cloud Only Detail Budget\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: add_budget, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 80,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"0001-2133-0000-5460-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 40, \"period\": \"Feb-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"0001-2133-0000-5640-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 40, \"period\": \"Feb-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\n\n### Multi-Turn: Completing a Transfer — Providing Destination and Period\nPrevious Entities: {\"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\", \"totalAmount\": 200, \"lines\": [{\"account\": \"1010-5670\", \"amount\": -200, \"period\": null}]}\nPrior assistant message: \"A destination budget account is needed to complete your transfer request...\"\nUser: \"To 1010-5940 in Feb-17\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: transfer_account, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 200,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5670\", \"amount\": -200, \"period\": \"Feb-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5940\", \"amount\": 200, \"period\": \"Feb-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\nNote: \"To 1010-5940\" = destination account. \"in Feb-17\" = period applied to ALL lines (source and destination). Source account and amount carried from Previous Entities. Period was null — now filled from current message for both lines.\n\n### Percentage Split Period Transfer\n\"Transfer $200 for 1010-5610 from Oct-17 to 70% Jun-17, 30% Jul-17 for Operating Budget from EPM\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: transfer_period, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\",\n    \"totalAmount\": 200,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5610\", \"amount\": -200, \"period\": \"Oct-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5610\", \"amount\": 140, \"period\": \"Jun-17\"},\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5610\", \"amount\": 60, \"period\": \"Jul-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\nNote: 70% of $200 = $140, 30% of $200 = $60. This is a percentage SPLIT of a known amount, NOT a balance-relative percentage. The account is the same on all lines because this is a period transfer. The amounts net to zero (-200 + 140 + 60 = 0).\n\n### Percentage Split with Account-First Phrasing\n\"For account 1010-5610 in Operating Budget from EPM, transfer $200 from Oct-17 with 70% to Jun-17 and 30% to Jul-17\"\n→ Same output as above. The account prefix applies to all lines.\n\n### List Budgets\n\"What control budgets do I have access to?\"\n→ actionType: list_budgets, intent: list_budgets, complete: true\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": null,\n    \"totalAmount\": 0,\n    \"lines\": []\n  },\n  \"complete\": true\n}\n```\n\n### List Budgets — Follow-up After Not Found\nChat history shows: \"The control budget \\\"Operating Budget\\\" was not found. You have access to: EPM Cloud Only Detail, Operating Budget from EPM + 3 more.\"\nUser: \"Show me all of them\"\n→ actionType: list_budgets, intent: list_budgets, complete: true\n\n### Review Request (NOT a help question)\n\"review budgetary control balances\"\n→ actionType: review, intent: review_balances\nNote: This is an ACTION request to review balances, not a question about reviewing. No question words present (no how/what/why/can). Route to review, not help.\n\n### Multi-Turn Review Continuation (resume review/deeplink flow)\nPrevious Entities: {\"control_budget_name\": null, \"totalAmount\": 0, \"lines\": [{\"account\": null, \"amount\": 0, \"period\": null}]}\nPrior assistant message: \"A control budget, budget account, and period are needed to review budgetary control balances...\"\nUser: \"Operating Budget from EPM, 1010-5670, Jan-17\"\n→ actionType: review, intent: review_balances, complete: true\nNote: This is a continuation of the pending review request. Preserve the prior review intent and merge the supplied control budget, account, and period instead of routing to help.\n\n### Multi-Turn Review Subtype Switch\nPrevious Entities: {\"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\", \"totalAmount\": 0, \"lines\": [{\"account\": \"1010-5940\", \"amount\": 0, \"period\": \"Feb-17\"}]}\nPrior assistant message: \"Here is the link to review budgetary control balances for Operating Budget from EPM, account 1010-5940, period Feb-17...\"\nUser: \"And the entries too\"\n→ actionType: review, intent: review_entries, complete: true\nNote: This is a continuation of the active review context, but the follow-up explicitly switches the subtype from balances to entries. Preserve the prior control budget, account, and period and change only the review intent.\n\n### Multi-Turn Review Subtype Switch (reverse)\nPrevious Entities: {\"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\", \"totalAmount\": 0, \"lines\": [{\"account\": \"1010-5940\", \"amount\": 0, \"period\": \"Feb-17\"}]}\nPrior assistant message: \"Here is the link to review budgetary control entries for Operating Budget from EPM, account 1010-5940, period Feb-17...\"\nUser: \"And the balances too\"\n→ actionType: review, intent: review_balances, complete: true\nNote: Preserve the same review entities and switch only the subtype back to balances.\n\n### Multi-Turn Review Account Correction\nPrevious Entities: {\"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\", \"totalAmount\": 0, \"lines\": [{\"account\": \"0001-1010-0000-5670-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 0, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"}]}\nPrior assistant message: \"The budget account provided has 6 segments, but Operating Budget from EPM has 2 segments: VSL Dept-VSL Account (e.g. XXXX-XXXX). Please provide the budget account in the correct format.\"\nUser: \"I think the account should be 1010-5670\"\n→ actionType: review, intent: review_balances, complete: true\nNote: This is a correction to the pending review request. Replace only the account with the corrected 2-segment value and preserve the prior control budget and period so the deeplink flow can continue.\n\n### Validation Correction Continuation (resume pending transfer)\nPrevious Entities: {\"control_budget_name\": \"Operating Budget from EPM\", \"totalAmount\": 4, \"lines\": [{\"account\": \"1010-5670\", \"amount\": -4, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"}, {\"account\": \"1010-5940\", \"amount\": 3, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"}]}\nPrior assistant message: \"The transfer amounts are not balanced. Source total: 4, destination total: 3. The amounts must be equal. Please adjust the amounts.\"\nUser: \"Use $4 for 1010-5940 instead\"\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: transfer_account, complete: true\nNote: This is a correction to the pending transfer_account request. Replace the destination amount, preserve the existing source line and period, and let downstream validation re-check the transfer.\n\n### Help\n\"How does budget checking work?\"\n→ actionType: help, intent: help\n\n### New Request After Completed Operation (DO NOT merge Previous Entities)\nPrevious Entities: {\"control_budget_name\": \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\", \"totalAmount\": 50, \"lines\": [{\"account\": \"0001-1010-0000-5660-000000-0000\", \"amount\": -50, \"period\": \"Jan-17\"}, {\"account\": \"0001-1010-0000-5660-000000-0000\", \"amount\": 50, \"period\": \"Feb-17\"}]}\nPrior assistant message: \"Budget Entry: BUDADJ ASSISTANT 13-MAR-2026 ... has been created. 50.00 USD has been transferred. <table>...</table>\"\nUser: \"Add $77 to 1010-5670 in May-17\"\n→ This is a NEW REQUEST (contains action verb \"Add\"). Do NOT carry forward Previous Entities. control_budget_name is null because it was not mentioned.\n→ actionType: budget_operation, intent: add_budget, complete: false\n```json\n{\n  \"entities\": {\n    \"control_budget_name\": null,\n    \"totalAmount\": 77,\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"account\": \"1010-5670\", \"amount\": 77, \"period\": \"May-17\"}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"complete\": false,\n  \"missing\": [\"control_budget_name\"],\n  \"followup\": \"Which control budget do you want to update?\"\n}\n```\nNote: Even though Previous Entities had \"EPM Cloud Only Detail\", this is a fresh request with its own action verb \"Add\". The budget name must come from the current message or be asked for.\n\n**Current User Message:** {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n**Additional Context:** {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.additional_context}}\n**History Message:** {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n**Previous Entities (from prior turn, may be empty):** {{$context.$variables.finXccVarConvEntities}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\":\"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"actionType\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"intent\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"complete\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"missing\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"followup\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"entities\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"control_budget_name\":{\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"totalAmount\":{\"type\":[\"number\",\"null\"]},\"lines\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\"}}},\"required\":[\"control_budget_name\",\"totalAmount\",\"lines\"]}},\"required\":[\"actionType\",\"intent\",\"entities\"]}"
        },
