          "id": "1771362330293",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771362330293_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a deterministic budget operations response formatter. Use ONLY the data provided below. Do NOT invent fields, reasons, or data not present in the inputs.\n\nUser request: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nIntent: {{$context.$variables.finXccVarConvIntent}}\nEntities: {{$context.$variables.finXccVarConvEntities}}\n\nPOST Response:\nBatchResultCode: {{$context.$variables.finXccVarConvPostResult.BatchResultCode}}\nBatchFatalErrorMessage: {{$context.$variables.finXccVarConvPostResult.BatchFatalErrorMessage}}\nTransactionNumber: {{$context.$variables.finXccVarConvPostResult.TransactionNumber}}\nSourceBudget: {{$context.$variables.finXccVarConvPostResult.SourceBudget}}\nProcessId: {{$context.$variables.finXccVarConvPostResult.ProcessId}}\n\nDetailed Result (pre-processed — deduplicated, sorted, stripped of metadata):\n{{$context.$variables.finXccVarConvProcessedResult}}\n\n=== FIELD KEY (compact format to save tokens) ===\nCB=ControlBudget, P=ControlBudgetPeriod, A=BudgetAccount, Amt=TransactionAmount, BR=BatchResult, HS=HeaderStatus, HR=HeaderResult, LS=LineStatus, LR=LineResult, AS=ActivityStatus, AR=ActivityResult, TB=TotalBudgetBalance, FA=FundsAvailableBalance, CC=ControlBudgetCurrency, BM=BudgetManager\nThe data is a JSON object with: rows (array of deduplicated/sorted items), count (original row count), dedupedCount (after dedup), batchResult, effectiveBatchResult, budgetManager, hasDisplayRows, errorMessage.\n\n=== FORMATTING RULES ===\n\nAll tables MUST use this exact HTML pattern for guaranteed visible borders:\n<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; border:1px solid #9e9e9e;\">\nAll <th> cells: style=\"background:#e0e0e0; border:1px solid #9e9e9e; padding:8px; text-align:left;\"\nAll <td> cells: style=\"border:1px solid #9e9e9e; padding:8px;\"\n\n=== RESPONSE LOGIC ===\n\n=== STATUS PRECEDENCE ===\nBefore choosing a response path, parse the Detailed Result JSON and derive EffectiveResult:\n- If Detailed Result effectiveBatchResult is FAIL, Failed, ERROR, or Error, use that value as EffectiveResult.\n- If Detailed Result batchResult is Failed or any row has BR, HS, LS, or AS containing Failed or Error, EffectiveResult is FAIL.\n- A detailed failure overrides POST BatchResultCode SUCCESS or WARNING. Never say money was added, reduced, or transferred when the Detailed Result failed.\n- Only use the SUCCESS or WARNING table path when EffectiveResult is SUCCESS or WARNING and the Detailed Result has at least one display row with CB, A, P, TB, or FA.\n- If Detailed Result has errorMessage, HR, LR, or AR, use those fields for the failure explanation.\n- Otherwise EffectiveResult is the POST BatchResultCode.\n\n**If EffectiveResult is \"ERROR\":**\n1. Start with: \"Budget adjustment could not be completed.\"\n2. Summarize the error in plain language using BatchFatalErrorMessage.\n3. Do NOT dump raw stack traces, package names, line numbers, SQL/PLSQL call stacks, or documentation URLs.\n4. If BatchFatalErrorMessage mentions \"ORA-00060\" or \"deadlock\", explain it as: another process was updating the same budget data at the same time, so Oracle stopped this request to prevent a conflict. Tell the user to retry after a short delay.\n5. For other errors, briefly explain the business-level issue if it is obvious from the message. Otherwise say that Oracle returned an error while processing the budget transaction.\n6. Give only 1-2 concise corrective actions. Do NOT give DBA-style debugging advice unless the user explicitly asks for technical details.\n7. After the explanation, show any available reference fields on separate lines in this order: Transaction #, Source Budget, Process ID. Omit any field that is empty.\n8. Do NOT show a table.\n\n**If EffectiveResult is \"SUCCESS\":**\n\n1. Confirmation line — format depends on intent:\n   - add_budget (positive amounts): \"Budget Entry: [TransactionNumber] has been created. [totalAmount] has been added.\"\n   - add_budget (negative amounts/reduce): \"Budget Entry: [TransactionNumber] has been created. [totalAmount] has been reduced.\"\n   - transfer_period: \"Budget Entry: [TransactionNumber] has been created. [totalAmount] has been transferred.\"\n   - transfer_account: \"Budget Entry: [TransactionNumber] has been created. [totalAmount] has been transferred.\"\n   Format the amount as a number with commas, followed by a space and the currency code from the Detailed Result’s ControlBudgetCurrency field (e.g. \"1,000.00 USD\"). Get totalAmount from Entities.\n\n   CRITICAL — The confirmation line MUST contain TWO sentences separated by a space:\n   Sentence 1: \"Budget Entry: [TransactionNumber] has been created.\"\n   Sentence 2: \"[totalAmount] has been [added/reduced/transferred].\"\n   Both sentences are REQUIRED. Do NOT skip the second sentence. Do NOT merge them into one.\n   WRONG: \"Budget Entry: BUDADJ ASSISTANT ... has been created. 1,000.00 USD\\n\\n<table...\"\n   RIGHT: \"Budget Entry: BUDADJ ASSISTANT ... has been created. 1,000.00 USD has been added.\\n\\n<table...\"\n\n2. Render ONE summary table with these columns in this EXACT order:\n   - Budget (ControlBudget field from Detailed Result — note this may differ from SourceBudget). **Make this a hyperlink** to the Review Budgetary Control Balances page using the deeplink URL pattern:\n     `/fscmUI/faces/deeplink?objType=XCC_REVIEWBUDGETBALANCES&action=NONE&objKey=controlBudgetName={budgetName};budgetAccount={account};periodName={period}`\n     Replace spaces in the budget name with `%20`. Use the Account and Budget Period from the SAME ROW. Open in new tab (`target=\"_blank\"`).\n   - Account (BudgetAccount)\n   - Budget Period (ControlBudgetPeriod)\n   - New Budget Balance (TotalBudgetBalance, formatted as amount + space + ControlBudgetCurrency from that row)\n   - New Funds Available (FundsAvailableBalance, formatted as amount + space + ControlBudgetCurrency from that row)\n\n   The rows in the Detailed Result are already deduplicated and sorted by the PROCESS_RESULT code node. Render ALL rows from the \"rows\" array as-is in the order provided. Use the compact field keys: CB=Budget name (for display and deeplink), A=Account, P=Period, TB=New Budget Balance, FA=New Funds Available, CC=Currency code.\n\n3. Do NOT repeat the transaction number below the table — it is already in the confirmation line above.\n\n**If EffectiveResult is \"FAIL\" and the Detailed Result rows array is empty (count is 0 or rows is []):**\nThe transaction failed but no per-line details are available. Show:\n1. \"Budget adjustment for [SourceBudget] failed.\"\n2. If the Detailed Result JSON contains an \"errorMessage\" field, display it.\n3. Otherwise display: \"No detailed results are available. You may not have data access to this control budget. Please contact your security manager or budget manager for access.\"\n4. Show Transaction # and Source Budget for reference.\nDo NOT attempt to render a table.\n\n**If EffectiveResult is \"FAIL\" and the Detailed Result rows array has data:**\n\n1. Status line: \"Budget adjustment failed.\"\n\n2. If hasDisplayRows is false, do NOT render a table; show \"Budget adjustment failed.\", then a \"Why it failed\" section using errorMessage, HeaderResult, LineResult, or ActivityResult. If hasDisplayRows is true, render the DETAILED RESULTS TABLE from the Detailed Result items array. Columns:\n   - Result (icon: ✔ green #2e7d32 for Passed, ✖ red #c62828 for Failed, ⚠ amber #f9a825 for Warning — based on LineStatus)\n   - Control Budget (ControlBudget)\n   - Budget Account (BudgetAccount)\n   - Period (ControlBudgetPeriod)\n   - Transaction Amount (TransactionAmount, formatted as signed amount + space + ControlBudgetCurrency from that row)\n   - Header Result (HeaderResult)\n   - Line Result (LineResult)\n   - Activity Result (ActivityResult)\n\n   The rows are already deduplicated and sorted. Render ALL rows from the \"rows\" array as-is. Use compact field keys: CB=Control Budget, A=Budget Account, P=Period, Amt=Transaction Amount, LS=LineStatus (for icon), HR=HeaderResult, LR=LineResult, AR=ActivityResult, CC=Currency code.\n\n3. After the table, add a \"Why it failed\" section:\n   - List the distinct errorMessage, HeaderResult, LineResult, and ActivityResult values from failed rows\n   - Suggest corrective action based on the failure reason (e.g., \"Insufficient funds — consider transferring budget from another account or period, or increasing the budget.\")\n\n4. Below, show:\n   - Transaction #: [TransactionNumber]\n   - Source Budget: [SourceBudget]\n   - Process ID: [ProcessId]\n\n**If EffectiveResult is \"WARNING\":**\nSame format as SUCCESS, but only when no detailed result row failed. Change the confirmation line to: \"Budget Entry: [TransactionNumber] has been created with warnings. [totalAmount] has been [added/transferred/reduced].\"\n\nKeep it concise. Format all monetary amounts as number with commas followed by a space and the currency code from ControlBudgetCurrency (e.g. \"1,000.00 USD\", \"-500.00 EUR\"). Do NOT use currency symbols like $ or €. Output raw HTML for tables (no markdown). Render every row from the \"rows\" array — the code node has already handled deduplication."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_FIN_XCC_BO_EPM_BUDGET_TRANSACTIONS",
            "functionName": "budgetaryControlResultsBudgetTransactions",
            "name": "call budgetaryControlResultsBudgetTransactions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "PROCESS_RESULT_NODE"
          },
          "code": "CALL_GETBUDGETTRANSACTIONRESULT",
          "id": "1771363111146",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771363129360_1",
              "name": "TransactionNumber",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.finXccVarConvTxnNumber}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1771363129361_2",
              "name": "SourceBudgetName",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.finXccVarConvSourceBudgetName}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Build Payload",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let entities = $context.$variables.finXccVarConvEntities || {};\nlet intent = $context.$variables.finXccVarConvIntent;\nlet segData = $context.$variables.finXccVarConvSegmentMappings;\nlet inputMessage = $context.$system.$inputMessage || \"\";\nlet priorValidation = $context.$variables.finXccVarConvValidationFollowup || \"\";\n\nlet clone = (value) => JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(value || {}));\nlet normalizedEntities = clone(entities);\n\nlet validPeriods = [];\nlet allPeriods = [];\nlet periodNameByLower = {};\nlet periodDataRaw = $context.$variables.finXccVarUqPeriodData;\nif (periodDataRaw) {\n  let pd = null;\n  if (typeof periodDataRaw === \"string\") {\n    try {\n      pd = JSON.parse(periodDataRaw);\n    } catch (e) {}\n  } else {\n    pd = periodDataRaw;\n  }\n  if (pd) {\n    validPeriods = pd.validPeriods || [];\n    allPeriods = pd.allPeriods || [];\n  }\n}\nfor (let i = 0; i < validPeriods.length; i++) {\n  if (validPeriods[i]) periodNameByLower[String(validPeriods[i]).toLowerCase()] = validPeriods[i];\n}\nfor (let i = 0; i < allPeriods.length; i++) {\n  let periodName = allPeriods[i] && allPeriods[i].periodName ? allPeriods[i].periodName : \"\";\n  if (periodName) periodNameByLower[String(periodName).toLowerCase()] = periodName;\n}\n\nlet parseAmount = (value) => {\n  if (value === null || value === undefined || value === \"\") return null;\n  let num = Number(String(value).replace(/,/g, \"\").trim());\n  return isNaN(num) ? null : num;\n};\n\nlet monthNames = [\"Jan\", \"Feb\", \"Mar\", \"Apr\", \"May\", \"Jun\", \"Jul\", \"Aug\", \"Sep\", \"Oct\", \"Nov\", \"Dec\"];\nlet monthIndex = {Jan: 1, Feb: 2, Mar: 3, Apr: 4, May: 5, Jun: 6, Jul: 7, Aug: 8, Sep: 9, Oct: 10, Nov: 11, Dec: 12};\n\nlet parsePeriod = (period) => {\n  if (!period || typeof period !== \"string\") return null;\n  let match = period.trim().match(/^([A-Za-z]{3})-(\\d{2})$/);\n  if (!match) return null;\n  let monKey = match[1].charAt(0).toUpperCase() + match[1].slice(1, 3).toLowerCase();\n  let mon = monthIndex[monKey];\n  if (!mon) return null;\n  return {month: mon, year: parseInt(match[2], 10)};\n};\n\nlet canonicalPeriodName = (period) => {\n  let key = String(period || \"\").toLowerCase();\n  return periodNameByLower[key] || period;\n};\n\nlet affirmativePattern = /^(yes|y|yep|yeah|correct|that'?s right|right|use that|that one|go ahead|proceed|submit|create it|create this|do it|confirm|confirmed)$/i;\nlet isAffirmativeSelection = (value) => affirmativePattern.test(String(value || \"\").trim());\nlet extractSuggestedPeriod = (text) => {\n  let raw = String(text || \"\").trim();\n  if (!raw) return \"\";\n  let match = raw.match(/Did you mean the budget period(?: of)? ([^?]+)\\?/i);\n  return match && match[1] ? match[1].trim() : \"\";\n};\nlet monthFullIndex = {\n  jan: 1, january: 1,\n  feb: 2, february: 2,\n  mar: 3, march: 3,\n  apr: 4, april: 4,\n  may: 5,\n  jun: 6, june: 6,\n  jul: 7, july: 7,\n  aug: 8, august: 8,\n  sep: 9, sept: 9, september: 9,\n  oct: 10, october: 10,\n  nov: 11, november: 11,\n  dec: 12, december: 12\n};\nlet compactPeriodPattern = /^[A-Za-z]{3}-\\d{2}$/;\nlet resolveSemanticPeriodName = (period) => {\n  let raw = String(period || \"\").trim();\n  if (!raw || compactPeriodPattern.test(raw)) return \"\";\n  let cleaned = raw.replace(/[,]+/g, \" \").replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim();\n  let match = cleaned.match(/^([A-Za-z]+)\\s+(\\d{2,4})$/) || cleaned.match(/^([A-Za-z]+)[-\\/](\\d{2,4})$/);\n  if (!match) return \"\";\n  let monthNumber = monthFullIndex[String(match[1] || \"\").toLowerCase()];\n  if (!monthNumber) return \"\";\n  let yy = String(match[2] || \"\").replace(/\\D/g, \"\").slice(-2);\n  if (!yy) return \"\";\n  return canonicalPeriodName(monthNames[monthNumber - 1] + \"-\" + yy);\n};\nlet suggestedPeriod = extractSuggestedPeriod(priorValidation);\nlet confirmedSuggestedPeriod = suggestedPeriod && isAffirmativeSelection(inputMessage);\n\nlet formatPeriod = (parsed) => canonicalPeriodName(monthNames[parsed.month - 1] + \"-\" + String(parsed.year).padStart(2, \"0\"));\n\nlet expandPeriodRange = (startPeriod, endPeriod) => {\n  let start = parsePeriod(startPeriod);\n  let end = parsePeriod(endPeriod);\n  if (!start || !end) return null;\n  let startKey = start.year * 12 + start.month;\n  let endKey = end.year * 12 + end.month;\n  if (endKey < startKey) return null;\n  let periods = [];\n  for (let cursor = startKey; cursor <= endKey; cursor++) {\n    let month = ((cursor - 1) % 12) + 1;\n    let year = Math.floor((cursor - month) / 12);\n    periods.push(formatPeriod({month: month, year: year}));\n  }\n  return periods;\n};\n\nlet getFiscalYearPeriods = (yearText) => {\n  let yy = String(yearText || \"\").replace(/\\D/g, \"\").slice(-2);\n  if (!yy) return null;\n  let periods = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < validPeriods.length; i++) {\n    let parsed = parsePeriod(validPeriods[i]);\n    if (parsed && String(parsed.year).padStart(2, \"0\") === yy) periods.push(canonicalPeriodName(validPeriods[i]));\n  }\n  if (periods.length > 0) return periods;\n  return expandPeriodRange(\"Jan-\" + yy, \"Dec-\" + yy);\n};\n\nlet buildRepeatedAddEntities = (message, existingEntities) => {\n  if (typeof message !== \"string\") return null;\n  let normalizedMessage = message.replace(/\\s+/g, \" \").trim().replace(/[.]+$/, \"\");\n  let sign = /\\b(remove|reduce|decrease|cut)\\b/i.test(normalizedMessage) ? -1 : 1;\n  let buildFromParts = (amountValue, accountValue, periods) => {\n    let amount = parseAmount(amountValue);\n    let account = accountValue ? String(accountValue).replace(/\\s/g, \"\") : \"\";\n    if ((amount === null || !account) && existingEntities.lines && existingEntities.lines.length > 0) {\n      if (amount === null) amount = parseAmount(existingEntities.lines[0].amount);\n      if (!account && existingEntities.lines[0].account) account = String(existingEntities.lines[0].account).replace(/\\s/g, \"\");\n    }\n    if (amount === null || !account || !periods || periods.length === 0) return null;\n    if (sign < 0 && amount > 0) amount = -amount;\n    let rebuilt = clone(existingEntities);\n    rebuilt.lines = [];\n    for (let p = 0; p < periods.length; p++) {\n      rebuilt.lines.push({account: account, amount: amount, period: periods[p]});\n    }\n    return rebuilt.lines.length > 0 ? rebuilt : null;\n  };\n\n  let amountMatch = normalizedMessage.match(/\\b(?:add|increase|adjust|remove|reduce|decrease|cut)\\s*\\$?\\s*([0-9][0-9,]*(?:\\.\\d+)?)/i);\n  let accountMatch = normalizedMessage.match(/\\b(?:account|acct)\\s+([0-9A-Za-z]+(?:-[0-9A-Za-z]+)+)\\b/i) || normalizedMessage.match(/\\bto\\s+([0-9A-Za-z]+(?:-[0-9A-Za-z]+)+)\\b/i);\n  let rangeMatch = normalizedMessage.match(/\\b(?:months?|periods?)\\s+(?:from\\s+)?([A-Za-z]{3}-\\d{2})\\s+(?:to|through)\\s+([A-Za-z]{3}-\\d{2})\\b/i)\n    || normalizedMessage.match(/\\bfrom\\s+([A-Za-z]{3}-\\d{2})\\s+(?:to|through)\\s+([A-Za-z]{3}-\\d{2})\\b/i)\n    || normalizedMessage.match(/\\b(?:in|for)\\s+([A-Za-z]{3}-\\d{2})\\s+(?:to|through)\\s+([A-Za-z]{3}-\\d{2})\\b/i);\n  if (rangeMatch) {\n    let periods = expandPeriodRange(rangeMatch[1], rangeMatch[2]);\n    let rebuilt = buildFromParts(amountMatch ? amountMatch[1] : null, accountMatch ? accountMatch[1] : null, periods);\n    if (rebuilt) return rebuilt;\n  }\n\n  let fyMatch = normalizedMessage.match(/\\ball\\s+months?\\s+in\\s+(?:fiscal\\s+year|fy)\\s+(\\d{2,4})\\b/i);\n  if (fyMatch) {\n    let periods = getFiscalYearPeriods(fyMatch[1]);\n    let rebuilt = buildFromParts(amountMatch ? amountMatch[1] : null, accountMatch ? accountMatch[1] : null, periods);\n    if (rebuilt) return rebuilt;\n  }\n\n  let clauseRegex = /\\b(?:add|increase|adjust|remove|reduce|decrease|cut)\\s*\\$?\\s*([0-9][0-9,]*(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s+to\\s+([0-9A-Za-z]+(?:-[0-9A-Za-z]+)+)\\s+in\\s+([A-Za-z]{3}-\\d{2})\\s+(?:to|through)\\s+([A-Za-z]{3}-\\d{2})\\b/gi;\n  let clauses = [];\n  let match = null;\n  while ((match = clauseRegex.exec(normalizedMessage)) !== null) {\n    clauses.push({amount: match[1], account: match[2], startPeriod: match[3], endPeriod: match[4]});\n  }\n  if (clauses.length === 0) return null;\n\n  let rebuilt = clone(existingEntities);\n  rebuilt.lines = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < clauses.length; i++) {\n    let clause = clauses[i];\n    let periods = expandPeriodRange(clause.startPeriod, clause.endPeriod);\n    let amount = parseAmount(clause.amount);\n    if (!periods || amount === null) return null;\n    if (sign < 0 && amount > 0) amount = -amount;\n    for (let p = 0; p < periods.length; p++) {\n      rebuilt.lines.push({account: clause.account.replace(/\\s/g, \"\"), amount: amount, period: periods[p]});\n    }\n  }\n  return rebuilt.lines.length > 0 ? rebuilt : null;\n};\n\nlet recomputeTotalAmount = (intentValue, lines, fallback) => {\n  if (!lines || lines.length === 0) return fallback;\n  let positive = 0;\n  let negative = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < lines.length; i++) {\n    let amt = parseAmount(lines[i].amount);\n    if (amt === null) continue;\n    if (amt >= 0) positive += amt;\n    else negative += Math.abs(amt);\n  }\n  if (intentValue === \"transfer_period\" || intentValue === \"transfer_account\") {\n    return positive > 0 ? positive : (negative || fallback);\n  }\n  if (positive > 0) return positive;\n  if (negative > 0) return negative;\n  return fallback;\n};\n\nif (intent === \"add_budget\") {\n  let rebuiltEntities = buildRepeatedAddEntities(inputMessage, normalizedEntities);\n  if (rebuiltEntities) {\n    normalizedEntities = rebuiltEntities;\n  }\n}\n\nlet normalizedIntent = intent;\nlet lowerMessage = inputMessage.toLowerCase();\nlet hasReductionVerb = /\\b(remove|reduce|decrease|cut)\\b/.test(lowerMessage);\nlet hasTransferCue = /\\b(transfer|move|reallocate|shift|redistribute|split|distribute)\\b/.test(lowerMessage);\nlet hasNegativeAmount = false;\nlet hasPositiveAmount = false;\nlet normalizedLines = normalizedEntities.lines || [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < normalizedLines.length; i++) {\n  let amt = parseAmount(normalizedLines[i].amount);\n  if (amt === null) continue;\n  if (amt < 0) hasNegativeAmount = true;\n  if (amt > 0) hasPositiveAmount = true;\n}\nif (normalizedIntent === \"transfer_period\" && hasReductionVerb && !hasTransferCue && hasNegativeAmount && !hasPositiveAmount) {\n  normalizedIntent = \"add_budget\";\n}\n\nnormalizedEntities.totalAmount = recomputeTotalAmount(normalizedIntent, normalizedLines, normalizedEntities.totalAmount);\n\nlet payloadLines = [];\nlet mappings = [];\nif (segData && segData.items && segData.items.length > 0 && segData.items[0].controlBudgetAccountSegments && segData.items[0].controlBudgetAccountSegments.items) {\n  let rawMappings = segData.items[0].controlBudgetAccountSegments.items;\n  for (let m = 0; m < rawMappings.length; m++) {\n    mappings.push({seq: rawMappings[m].displaySequenceNumber, source: rawMappings[m].sourceSegmentColumnName});\n  }\n  mappings.sort((a, b) => a.seq - b.seq);\n}\nfor (let i = 0; i < normalizedLines.length; i++) {\n  let line = normalizedLines[i];\n  let segments = String(line.account || \"\").replace(/\\s/g, \"\").split(\"-\");\n  let periodName = canonicalPeriodName(line.period);\n  if (periodName === line.period) {\n    let semanticPeriodName = resolveSemanticPeriodName(line.period);\n    if (semanticPeriodName && semanticPeriodName !== line.period) {\n      periodName = semanticPeriodName;\n    } else if (confirmedSuggestedPeriod && !compactPeriodPattern.test(String(line.period || \"\").trim())) {\n      periodName = canonicalPeriodName(suggestedPeriod);\n    }\n  }\n  line.period = periodName;\n  let lineObj = {\n    \"LineNumber\": String(i + 1),\n    \"Amount\": String(line.amount),\n    \"CurrencyCode\": \"USD\",\n    \"PeriodName\": periodName\n  };\n  if (mappings.length > 0 && mappings.length === segments.length) {\n    for (let s = 0; s < segments.length; s++) {\n      let glSegment = mappings[s].source;\n      let segNum = glSegment.replace(\"SEGMENT\", \"\");\n      lineObj[\"Segment\" + segNum] = segments[s];\n    }\n  } else {\n    for (let s = 0; s < segments.length; s++) {\n      lineObj[\"Segment\" + String(s + 1)] = segments[s];\n    }\n  }\n  payloadLines.push(lineObj);\n}\n\nlet payloadObj = {\"Lines\": payloadLines};\nlet dt = $context.$system.$currentDateTime;\nlet months = [\"JAN\", \"FEB\", \"MAR\", \"APR\", \"MAY\", \"JUN\", \"JUL\", \"AUG\", \"SEP\", \"OCT\", \"NOV\", \"DEC\"];\nlet dtYear = dt.substring(0, 4);\nlet dtMonth = parseInt(dt.substring(5, 7), 10);\nlet dtDay = parseInt(dt.substring(8, 10), 10);\nlet dtHour = parseInt(dt.substring(11, 13), 10);\nlet dtMin = dt.substring(14, 16);\nlet dtSec = dt.substring(17, 19);\nlet ampm = dtHour >= 12 ? \"PM\" : \"AM\";\nlet h12 = dtHour % 12;\nif (h12 === 0) h12 = 12;\nlet txnNumber = \"BUDADJ ASSISTANT \" + dtDay + \"-\" + months[dtMonth - 1] + \"-\" + dtYear + \" \" + h12 + \":\" + dtMin + \":\" + dtSec + ampm + \" UTC\";\n\nreturn {\n  \"requestBody\": {\n    \"SourceBudget\": normalizedEntities.control_budget_name,\n    \"TransactionNumber\": txnNumber,\n    \"BudgetTransactionType\": \"ADJUST_BUDGET\",\n    \"BudgetAmountsMode\": \"INCREMENT\",\n    \"BatchFundsAction\": \"RESERVE\",\n    \"BudgetTransactionPayload\": JSON.stringify(payloadObj)\n  },\n  \"txnNumber\": txnNumber,\n  \"sourceBudgetName\": normalizedEntities.control_budget_name,\n  \"entities\": normalizedEntities,\n  \"intent\": normalizedIntent\n};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "UNIFIED_CALL_CREATE"
          },
          "code": "BUILD_PAYLOAD",
          "id": "UNIFIED_BUILD_PAYLOAD",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "businessObjectCode": "ORA_FIN_XCC_BO_EPM_BUDGET_TRANSACTIONS",
            "functionName": "budgetaryControlBudgetTransactions",
            "name": "Call budgetaryControlBudgetTransactions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "UNIFIED_SAVE_POST"
          },
          "code": "CALL_CREATEBUDGETTRANSACTION",
          "id": "UNIFIED_CALL_CREATE",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "UCC_1",
              "name": "SourceBudgetName",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_PAYLOAD.$output.result.sourceBudgetName}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "UCC_2",
              "name": "TransactionNumber",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_PAYLOAD.$output.result.requestBody.TransactionNumber}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "UCC_3",
              "name": "BudgetTransactionType",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_PAYLOAD.$output.result.requestBody.BudgetTransactionType}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "UCC_4",
              "name": "BudgetAmountsMode",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.BUILD_PAYLOAD.$output.result.requestBody.BudgetAmountsMode}}"
            },
